---
description: Initialize C++ members in the constructor initializer list before the body runs
globs: **/*.{h,hpp,cpp}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Initialize members before the constructor body

If the constructor body (or helpers it calls) **reads** a member, initialize that member in the constructor initializer list. Do not rely on later setters, or on the reader noticing an in-class default.

Uninitialized scalars and pointers are undefined behavior. Even with in-class defaults, the init list makes the starting state visible at the construction site.

```cpp
// BAD — applyUiStrings() / refreshFromSession() read these before setTagSession()
PresentationPanel::PresentationPanel(QWidget* parent) : QWidget(parent) {
  buildUi();
  applyUiStrings();
}

// GOOD
PresentationPanel::PresentationPanel(QWidget* parent)
    : QWidget(parent),
      tagSession_(nullptr),
      selectedTagIndexSet_(),
      currentTagSessionIndex_(-1),
      populatingRows_(false) {
  buildUi();
  applyUiStrings();
}
```

Keep in-class `= nullptr` / `= -1` / `= false` as a second line of defense. Init-list order must match declaration order.
